Prior work RidgeFill builds on:
  - DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash's Causal Encoder-Decoder (DeepSeek technical report,
    arXiv:2609.19969, §2.2): the decoder's global KV cache is built from the encoder's
    outputs, so most prompt tokens skip the full decoder computation during prefill.
  - YOCO, "You Only Cache Once: Decoder-Decoder Architectures for Language Models"
    (Sun et al., 2024, arXiv:2405.05254): one KV cache, produced by the first half of the
    model, serves the second half, so prefill can exit early.
  - kishida's Q3-8B-KVA-Projector, "Late Layer KV Approximation Projector for Qwen3-8B"
    (https://huggingface.co/kishida/Q3-8B-KVA-Projector): the first retrofit of the idea
    onto an existing model, with a projector that approximates late layers' K/V. "KVA" is
    that work's name; this project used it as a working name only.

What RidgeFill adds: a closed-form ridge fit with no gradient training; maps to the
late layers' INPUTS, so each late layer computes its own K/V and recurrent state; an
exact tail of prompt tokens; exact-row selection; a correction of the recurrent
(gated delta net) state; and a plugin for the radiance inference engine.
